Z||000000||mbramble||04-24-2001||08:08 PM||||Is the little push switch located near the door latch "post" on an 85 basically the same thing as the ajar switch that is mounted inside the door latch on an 87??<P>Is there an ajar switch on the 85's rear deck lid??  It is part of the trunk latch of my 87 but the 85 seems to be different.<P>Thanks,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-24-2001||09:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mbramble:<BR><B>Is the little push switch located near the door latch "post" on an 85 basically the same thing as the ajar switch that is mounted inside the door latch on an 87??<P>Is there an ajar switch on the 85's rear deck lid??  It is part of the trunk latch of my 87 but the 85 seems to be different.<P>Thanks,<BR>Mike</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, to your first question.  The door pin switch is for the dome lights, while there is a switch inside the latch for the AJAR light.  At least that is how your 87 is.  Im not sure whether there is also a latch switch in your 85 along with the pin switch, or if the pin switch also controls the ajar light.<P>So, turn the ignition on, open your door, and then push in the pin switch.  If your dome lights go out but your AJAR light still stays on, then it works like the 87 does.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Fiero87311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto near completion!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
